### Departments API v1. Reads are anonymous; changes send X-Acting-User-Id (temporary stand-in for authentication; 1 = seeded super admin, 2 = seeded admin).
### Select the "local" environment (http/http-client.env.json). Run requests top to bottom.

### List all departments
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/departments
Accept: application/json

### Create a department
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/departments
X-Acting-User-Id: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Cutting",
  "code": "CUTTING",
  "description": "Cuts printed sheets"
}

### Get the department created above
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/departments/{{create.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### Update name and description (code is immutable)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/departments/{{create.response.body.$.id}}
X-Acting-User-Id: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Cutting and Trimming",
  "description": "Cuts and trims printed sheets"
}

### Deactivate the department (soft delete)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/departments/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/deactivate
X-Acting-User-Id: 1

### List the roles of department 2 (Admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/departments/2/roles

### Assign roles to a department (replaces; its users inherit them)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/departments/2/roles
X-Acting-User-Id: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roles": ["Admin"]
}

### Failure: department with an unknown role
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/departments/2/roles
X-Acting-User-Id: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roles": ["Wizard"]
}

### Failure: invalid body
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/departments
X-Acting-User-Id: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "code": "bad code"
}

### Failure: unknown department
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/departments/999999

### Failure: unknown API version
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/departments
